{"id": "Deo0BU_xNwU", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why did Narad Muni CURSE Lord Vishnu? 🐒 He asked Vishnu for his handsome face… and walked into a swayamvara with a MONKEY'S.\n\nNarad Muni sat in tapas by the Ganga. Indra sent Kamadeva to break it, and every flower arrow failed. Narad was so proud he ran to tell Shiva. Shiva said: \"Never tell this to Vishnu.\" So of course… he told Vishnu. 😅\n\nVishnu saw a tree of pride sprouting in his devotee's heart, and decided to uproot it. A magic city appeared on Narad's path. Its princess, Vishwamohini, was choosing a husband, and her palm said whoever weds her will never die. The sage who beat desire fell in love in seconds.\n\n\"Hari, give me your looks!\" Vishnu promised to do what was truly best for him… and gave him a monkey's face. (In Sanskrit, \"Hari\" means Vishnu, and also a monkey!) Shiva's ganas giggled, the princess wouldn't look at him, and she garlanded Vishnu, who came as a king.\n\nNarad saw his face in the water and cursed Vishnu: be born a human, suffer separation from your wife, and need monkeys to help you. Vishnu smiled and accepted. That curse became the Ramayana: Ram, Sita, and Hanuman's vanara army. 🙏\n\nHe beat desire… but lost to pride.\n\n📖 As told in the Ramcharitmanas (Bal Kand) by Goswami Tulsidas; the same story is in the Shiva Purana (Rudra Samhita).\n\n🎉 Our 15K FAMILY DEAL: Rishi Katha Books 1–3, the set of 3 for just ₹350 (₹500), only till 21 Oct, midnight!\nComment FAMILY and we'll DM you the deal, or tap the link in bio → rishikatha.com\n\nIs your name HARI, NARAYAN or VISHNU? Comment it below! 👇 Save this for story time, and share it with someone who brags a little too much 😄\n\n#NaradMuni #Narad #Vishnu #LordVishnu #Narayan #Ramayana #Ramcharitmanas #HinduMythology #IndianMythology #MythologyForKids #Hanuman #SanatanDharma #RishiKatha #KidsBooks #StoryTime", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 179233